Compare paths case-insensitively with libgit2's own functions on Windows.

The index sorted and searched its entries with _stricmp, the working
tree iterator with git__strcasecmp. On Windows ARM64 the C runtime's
_stricmp orders bytes from 0x80 differently, so with core.ignorecase a
non-ASCII path in the index never met its file on disk: status showed
it deleted and untracked at once. One comparison on both sides.

--- a/src/util/win32/msvc-compat.h
+++ b/src/util/win32/msvc-compat.h
@@ -18,8 +18,10 @@
 # define SSIZE_MAX LONG_MAX
 #endif
 
-#define strcasecmp(s1, s2) _stricmp(s1, s2)
-#define strncasecmp(s1, s2, c) _strnicmp(s1, s2, c)
+extern int git__strcasecmp(const char *a, const char *b);
+extern int git__strncasecmp(const char *a, const char *b, size_t sz);
+#define strcasecmp(s1, s2) git__strcasecmp(s1, s2)
+#define strncasecmp(s1, s2, c) git__strncasecmp(s1, s2, c)
 
 #endif
 
